---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretBaselineResult = await interpretBaseline(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const translateObjectivesResult = await translateObjectives(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretBaselineResult.accepted);
const constructInterventionsResult = await constructInterventions(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, translateObjectivesResult.accepted);
const planMonitoringResult = await planMonitoring(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructInterventionsResult.accepted);
const adaptManagementResult = await adaptManagement(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planMonitoringResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretBaseline: interpretBaselineResult, translateObjectives: translateObjectivesResult, constructInterventions: constructInterventionsResult, planMonitoring: planMonitoringResult, adaptManagement: adaptManagementResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretBaselineResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...translateObjectivesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructInterventionsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planMonitoringResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...adaptManagementResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretBaselineResult.checks, ...translateObjectivesResult.checks, ...constructInterventionsResult.checks, ...planMonitoringResult.checks, ...adaptManagementResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A sensitive species location is recorded: restrict exact coordinates in public and volunteer views. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (restrict exact coordinates in public and volunteer views.) through the existing stage result for HabitatObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior HabitatObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A survey is conducted in a different season: flag comparability before interpreting change. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (flag comparability before interpreting change.) through the existing stage result for HabitatObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior HabitatObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Land access permission expires: stop affected field tasks immediately. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (stop affected field tasks immediately.) through the existing stage result for HabitatObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior HabitatObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — An intervention has an unexpected effect: preserve the observation and trigger expert review. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve the observation and trigger expert review.) through the existing stage result for HabitatObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior HabitatObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Volunteer effort varies: record sampling effort alongside observations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (record sampling effort alongside observations.) through the existing stage result for HabitatObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior HabitatObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretBaseline: interpretBaselineResult, translateObjectives: translateObjectivesResult, constructInterventions: constructInterventionsResult, planMonitoring: planMonitoringResult, adaptManagement: adaptManagementResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
